Licences of the code in the dseams source package

dseams itself, meaning the R code, the C and C++ glue in src/*.c and
src/*.cpp, configure, cleanup and tools/, is under the MIT licence; see
LICENSE. The d-SEAMS engine copied into src/seams is also MIT, by the
d-SEAMS core team.

The source package also carries readcon-core, the Rust crates it builds
with, and chemfiles with the libraries chemfiles bundles. Each keeps its
own licence, listed below with the path of its licence text inside the
source package. Every licence here allows redistribution in source form
alongside MIT code. Where a part offers a choice ("A OR B"), dseams
redistributes it under either. inst/AUTHORS names the authors of each
part.


